From 112dc746a70f8d53d74e4effa77b97487042ed79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ethan Kiczek <ekiczek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Feb 2026 02:32:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use Mitsubishi's actual F/C lookup table instead of standard
 math
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Standard rounding (nearest 0.5°C) diverges from Mitsubishi's own
Fahrenheit-to-Celsius mapping at several points:
  64-66°F: Mitsubishi maps 0.5°C lower than standard math
  69-72°F: Mitsubishi maps 0.5°C higher than standard math

This caused HA to display different temperatures than the Comfort app
and the physical thermostat (e.g., setting 69°F from HA sent 20.5°C,
but Mitsubishi maps 69°F = 21°C).

The lookup table was derived by testing every Fahrenheit value (61-80°F)
on the Comfort app and recording the Celsius value the API received.
Values outside the table range fall back to standard math (primarily
for current room temperature readings).
