+From 21ec51210342eebbd4ffd006e3c15631af4f23fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Ethan Kiczek <ekiczek@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Tue, 24 Feb 2026 21:20:39 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] Fix Fahrenheit display precision with proper C/F conversion
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+Mitsubishi systems use 0.5°C steps internally. Previously, the integration
+reported temperatures in Celsius and let HA convert to Fahrenheit, which
+caused up to 1°F rounding drift (e.g., 69°F setpoint displayed as 70°F).
+
+Changes:
+- Add _c_to_f() and _f_to_c() conversion helpers that handle 0.5°C steps
+- Switch entity to report in Fahrenheit directly (UnitOfTemperature.FAHRENHEIT)
+- Convert all temperature readings (current, target, min, max) from API
+  Celsius to Fahrenheit using our precise rounding
+- Convert user-set temperatures from Fahrenheit to nearest 0.5°C for API
+- Change temperature step from 0.5°C to 1°F
+
+When setting temperatures via HA, the conversion is now:
+  69°F -> 20.5°C (API) -> displays as 69°F ✓
+Previously: 69°F -> 20.56°C -> HA rounds to 21°C -> displays as 70°F ✗
+
+Note: Temperatures set via the Comfort app may still show 1°F off in HA
+due to the Comfort app's own rounding to whole Celsius degrees.
